---
// src/pages/index.astro · 1014 V21
// V21 (Homepage — Watchman's Desk and YouTube redesign, Dutch 1014): the Desk is
// a dispatch log — the last three letters/briefs as full-width rows (dateline +
// type stamp, title + deck, call to action), newest row taller with its red
// strapline, a faint watchtower behind the masthead. YouTube leaves the Desk for
// its own film-strip band below it: channel + Subscribe on the left, the latest
// six uploads on a sideways reel, pulled at build time from the channel's RSS
// (src/lib/youtube-feed.js; falls back to the last good list). The hand-edited
// latestVideo const is gone. Order: hero → Featured Picks → Last 30 Days →
// Watchman's Desk → YouTube → Close to the Hip.
// V20 (Featured Picks — 10 slots, Dutch 1013): up to ten picks, one per
// category (src/lib/home-pieces.js V5) — two rows of five on desktop, same card
// size; rows of three on a tablet; one column on a phone.
// V19 (spec 1012 V4): hero shorter (narrower picture panel, 105px picture,
// tighter spacing); Doctrines and Published Books level on one row, each with
// its subline beneath ("Where Christianity Has Been Handed a Lie" → /books);
// Last 30 Days subline rewritten, gold chevron + SEE LIST / HIDE LIST cue.
// V18 (Homepage Featured and Recent Spec 1012 V3): the large Doctrines card is
// gone — the mustard Start Here button carries it, with a small "The Old Paths ·
// The Departure" line beneath; Featured Picks is five compact cards in one row
// (symbol, menu location line, title, deck, CTA + date); each Last 30 Days row
// shows its category symbol. Order: hero → Featured → Last 30 Days → Desk → CttH.
// V17: the slim FeastHero leads the page on a feast day (Feast Day Hero Brief
// 1011 V2); nothing renders on other days.
// V16: the page centers on new work (Homepage Featured and Recent Spec 1011 V2).
// The six-tab rail is gone — its card looks now live in src/data/series-skins.js
// and render through SeriesCard — and so is the old five-link Featured Picks
// strip (the featured-queue rotation). Order: hero → Doctrines card (with The
// Old Paths and The Departure side by side) → Featured Picks (hand-picked via
// `featured`/`featuredAt`, six seats, each card in its series skin; hidden when
// none) → Last 30 Days (closed dropdowns per section, from src/lib/
// home-pieces.js; hidden when empty) → Watchman's Desk → Close to the Hip.
// V15: the /on-these-two rail card reads The Paper Trail (address unchanged),
// matching the page title and the Counterfeits menu.
// V14: the hero headline, its italic, the eyebrow and the body paragraph get dark-mode
// colours; they had none, so the headline sat near-black on the dark page.
// V13: the Cosmology rail card opens the /cosmology section front, matching the
// Header slot; The Heavens and the Earth moved out of the blog to
// /cosmology/the-heavens-and-the-earth. Copy unchanged.
// V12: the Restoration rail's Cosmology placeholder goes live, pointing at The
// Heavens and the Earth (/blog/the-heavens-and-the-earth) — same target as the
// Header's Cosmology slot (Header V8). DRAFT badge, Placeholder eyebrow and
// Coming soon line go with it; the description is the approved copy, kept as is.
// No placeholders are left in the rail.
// V11: the What They Buried rail loses its Living Temple placeholder and gains
// the Investigations section card (/investigations). The Living Temple is live —
// 5 of 5 pieces — so nothing on this page may call it draft or coming soon. The
// DRAFT badge, the Placeholder eyebrow and the Coming soon line go with the tile.
// Cosmology is now the only placeholder left in the rail.
// V10: latestVideo swapped to the second Dutchman upload — "The Nation Is Not
// the Church" (the Wicked Husbandmen). Title + url only; the card is untouched.
// V9: the Dutchman channel card in the Watchman's Desk carries a small
// "Latest: <video>" line under "Visit the channel". It is edited in ONE place
// — the `latestVideo` const just below — and set to null to hide the line.
// The card is now a <div> holding two links (a link cannot nest inside a
// link); the channel link keeps every class and style it had.
// V8: latest-insight strip breaks postedDate ties by id descending, so same-day
// insights surface the highest id (SI-003 over SI-002) deterministically.
// V7: added the "On These Two" walker card to the False Foundations rail group
// (fifth item; no new group). Deck line per spec; not in Featured Picks.
// V6: strip now links to /close-to-the-hip (the renamed page). Still INSIGHTS
// ONLY — never a Defense entry — and still renders nothing when none is posted.
// V5: added the quiet Scripture Insight strip below the Watchman's Desk — the
// latest posted insight (same JSON + posted-only filter as the insights lane),
// or nothing at all when no entry is posted (no empty container).
// Watchman's Desk band renders the two most recent entries (featuredEntries,
// derived from sortDate — see the data file) as equal, side-by-side WatchmanCards
// (featured variant). Neither is primary; the "Browse the archive" link is a
// band-level affordance, not carried inside either card.
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SeriesCard from '../components/SeriesCard.astro';
import Symbol from '../components/Symbol.astro';
import FeastHero from '../components/FeastHero.jsx';
import { sortedEntries, KINDS } from '../data/watchmans-desk.js';
import { latestVideos, CHANNEL_URL } from '../lib/youtube-feed.js';
import { homePieces, featuredPicks, recentGroups, showDate } from '../lib/home-pieces.js';

// ── SCRIPTURE INSIGHT (strip) — the single latest posted insight, read at build
// time from the same JSON the /close-to-the-hip insights lane uses, with the SAME
// posted-only filter (so a withdrawn entry never surfaces). Newest first by
// postedDate; take one. Null when nothing is posted → the strip renders nothing.
const siRaw = fs.readFileSync(path.join(process.cwd(), 'public/data/scripture-insights.json'), 'utf-8');
const latestInsight = JSON.parse(siRaw).insights
  .filter((i) => i.status === 'posted')
  .sort((a, b) =>
    String(b.postedDate).localeCompare(String(a.postedDate)) ||
    String(b.id).localeCompare(String(a.id)))[0] ?? null;

// ── THE WATCHMAN'S DESK (dispatch log) — the three most recent entries by
// sortDate, newest first, straight from the data file. The newest is the lead
// row (larger title + its red strapline). Every entry has a reader page.
const MONTHS = ['JAN', 'FEB', 'MAR', 'APR', 'MAY', 'JUN', 'JUL', 'AUG', 'SEP', 'OCT', 'NOV', 'DEC'];
const dateline = (iso) => { const [y, m, d] = iso.split('-'); return `${+d} ${MONTHS[+m - 1]} ${y}`; };
const deskLog = sortedEntries.slice(0, 3).map((e) => ({
  href: `/watchmans-desk/${e.slug}`,
  title: e.title,
  deck: e.deck,
  tagline: e.strapline || '',
  dateline: dateline(e.sortDate),
  kind: KINDS[e.kind] || 'LETTER',
  cta: e.kind === 'field-brief' ? 'Read the Brief' : 'Read the Letter',
}));

// ── YOUTUBE (film strip) — the latest uploads, pulled from the channel's public
// RSS feed at build time (src/lib/youtube-feed.js); never empty — it falls back
// to the last good list.
const videos = await latestVideos();


// ── FEATURED PICKS + LAST 30 DAYS — one pool (src/lib/home-pieces.js). Picks
// come first so Last 30 Days can leave them out; nothing shows twice.
const pieces = await homePieces();
const picks = featuredPicks(pieces);
const recent = recentGroups(pieces, picks);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nazaryah - Biblical Studies with Scholarly Integrity"
  description="Explore Scripture through original languages, fresh perspectives, and rich historical context. A modern biblical studies platform for serious learners."
>
  <!-- Feast mode (Feast Day Hero Brief 1011 V2): the slim hero, first on the
       page, on a feast day only. On any other day it renders nothing. -->
  <FeastHero client:load variant="slim" />

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero-section relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Subtle grid texture overlay -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true" style="
      background-image:
        repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, transparent, transparent 39px, rgba(0,0,0,0.022) 40px),
        repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, transparent 39px, rgba(0,0,0,0.022) 40px);
      z-index: 0;
    "></div>

    <div class="hero-grid relative z-10">
      <!-- LEFT: Logo panel (dark background matches logo image) -->
      <div class="logo-panel">
        <img
          src="/images/nazaryah-logo.png"
          alt="Nazaryah — Separated Unto Yah"
          class="logo-panel-img"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- RIGHT: Content -->
      <div class="content-panel">
        <div class="hero-eyebrow">Separated Unto Yahuah</div>
        <h1 class="hero-headline">
          The doctrine was built to keep you <em>comfortable.</em>
        </h1>
        <div class="hero-rule"></div>
        <div class="hero-body-row">
          <p class="hero-body">
            Nazaryah goes back to the source — original languages, restored names, and the Torah your church quietly skipped. No denominations. No comfortable answers. Just the text.
          </p>
          <!-- Two buttons on one row, centres level; each subline under its own
               button (spec 1012 V4, A3/A4). On a phone: button, line, button, line. -->
          <div class="hero-cta-stack">
            <a href="/doctrines" class="hero-cta hero-cta--doctrines" aria-label="Start here — Doctrines">
              <span class="hero-cta-badge"><span class="star" aria-hidden="true">★</span> Start Here</span>
              <span class="hero-cta-label">Doctrines</span>
              <span class="hero-cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/books" class="hero-cta hero-cta--ghost" aria-label="Read — Published Books">
              <span class="hero-cta-badge"><span class="star" aria-hidden="true">★</span> Read</span>
              <span class="hero-cta-label">Published Books</span>
              <span class="hero-cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
            <p class="hero-doc-links hero-sub--doctrines">
              <a href="/doctrines/old-paths">The Old Paths</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/doctrines/the-departure">The Departure</a>
            </p>
            <p class="hero-doc-links hero-sub--books">
              <a href="/books">Where Christianity Has Been Handed a Lie</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero-section {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.3rem 1.5rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .hero-grid {
      display: grid;
      /* V4 (A5): the dark logo panel narrows so the parchment side gains width. */
      grid-template-columns: 7fr 18fr;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 80rem;
      /* Aspect ratio dropped — the second stacked CTA needs vertical room
         and the box now sizes to its content. min-height keeps the box
         from collapsing on copy changes. */
      min-height: 8rem;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-radius: 4px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.22), 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
    }

    /* ── LEFT PANEL: dark, logo centered ── */
    .logo-panel {
      position: relative;
      background: #0f0a04;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    /* Subtle warm radial glow behind the logo */
    .logo-panel::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 45%, rgba(180, 120, 30, 0.18) 0%, transparent 70%);
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    /* Corner ornaments */
    .logo-panel::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 10px; left: 10px;
      width: 20px; height: 20px;
      border-top: 1.5px solid rgba(196, 154, 78, 0.45);
      border-left: 1.5px solid rgba(196, 154, 78, 0.45);
    }

    .logo-panel-img {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      width: 100%;
      height: 105px; /* V4 (A5): three quarters of 140px */
      object-fit: contain;
    }

    /* ── RIGHT PANEL ── */
    .content-panel {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 0.08rem;
      padding: 0.2rem 2rem;
    }

    .hero-eyebrow {
      color: #6b4d12;
      font-family: var(--font-display, 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .hero-eyebrow::before {
      content: '\25C6  '; /* ◆ */
      color: #d4a531;
    }

    .hero-headline {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.45rem);
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.005em;
      color: var(--color-primary-text);
      margin: 0;
    }

    .hero-headline em {
      font-style: italic;
      color: #6b4d12;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .hero-rule {
      width: 50px;
      height: 2px;
      background: #d4a531;
      opacity: 0.85;
      margin-top: 0.1rem;
    }

    /* Body + CTA share one horizontal row so the button hangs to the
       right of the paragraph instead of dropping below the hero box. */
    .hero-body-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.3rem;
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .hero-body {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      line-height: 1.38;
      color: var(--color-secondary-text);
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      max-width: 44rem;
      margin: 0;
    }

    :global(.dark) .hero-headline { color: var(--color-dark-text); }
    :global(.dark) .hero-headline em,
    :global(.dark) .hero-eyebrow { color: var(--gold-light); }
    :global(.dark) .hero-body { color: var(--color-dark-secondary-text); }

    /* Vertical stack for the two CTAs — primary on top, ghost secondary
       beneath. Aligned to the start of the column so both buttons start
       at the same left edge. */
    /* Row 1: the two buttons, centres level. Row 2: their sublines, level. */
    .hero-cta-stack {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto auto;
      grid-template-areas: "doc books" "docsub bookssub";
      align-items: center;
      justify-items: center;
      column-gap: 0.7rem;
      row-gap: 0.12rem;
      align-self: flex-start;
    }
    .hero-cta--doctrines { grid-area: doc; }
    .hero-cta--ghost { grid-area: books; }
    .hero-sub--doctrines { grid-area: docsub; }
    .hero-sub--books { grid-area: bookssub; }

    /* The mustard button with the paired-documents line directly beneath it. */
    .hero-doc-links {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display, 'Cinzel', Georgia, serif); font-size: 0.66rem;
      font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; font-variant: small-caps; color: #3a2a12;
    }
    .hero-doc-links a { color: #3a2a12; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(107, 77, 18, 0.35); }
    .hero-doc-links a:hover { color: #6b4d12; border-bottom-color: #6b4d12; }
    :global(.dark) .hero-doc-links, :global(.dark) .hero-doc-links a { color: var(--gold-light); }

    /* ── "Start Here · Doctrines" CTA — single gold pill with badge inside ── */
    .hero-cta {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.7rem;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      align-self: center;
      padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f0c450 0%, #d4a531 100%);
      color: #1a0e06;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-family: var(--font-display, 'Cinzel', 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif);
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      border: 2px solid #a87f1f;
      border-radius: 4px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px -2px rgba(168, 127, 31, 0.45);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
    }
    .hero-cta:hover {
      transform: translateY(-1px);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #d4a531 0%, #a87f1f 100%);
      box-shadow: 0 6px 16px -2px rgba(168, 127, 31, 0.55);
    }

    .hero-cta-badge {
      background: #1a0e06;
      color: #f0c450;
      font-size: 0.62rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      font-weight: 700;
      padding: 0.32rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .hero-cta-badge .star {
      margin-right: 0.2rem;
    }

    .hero-cta-label {
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #1a0e06;
    }
    .hero-cta-arrow {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1;
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .hero-cta:hover .hero-cta-arrow {
      transform: translateX(3px);
    }

    /* Ghost variant — same compound shape as primary but transparent
       background with a gold outline. Visually subordinate so Doctrines
       stays the dominant "Start Here" entry point. */
    .hero-cta--ghost {
      background: transparent;
      border-color: #a87f1f;
      color: #6b4d12;
      padding: 0.48rem 1.2rem;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      box-shadow: none;
    }
    .hero-cta--ghost .hero-cta-badge {
      background: #1a0e06;
      color: #f0c450;
      font-size: 0.55rem;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;
    }
    .hero-cta--ghost .hero-cta-label,
    .hero-cta--ghost .hero-cta-arrow {
      color: #6b4d12;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
    .hero-cta--ghost:hover {
      transform: translateY(-1px);
      background: rgba(168, 127, 31, 0.1);
      border-color: #6b4d12;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 10px -3px rgba(168, 127, 31, 0.3);
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .hero-section {
        padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
      }

      .hero-grid {
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        aspect-ratio: unset;
        max-width: 100%;
      }
      /* The panel may shrink to the column: the mustard button's tracked caps
         used to push it 46px past the box on a phone, clipping the text. */
      .content-panel { min-width: 0; }
      .hero-cta-stack {
        max-width: 100%;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, auto);
        grid-template-areas: "doc" "docsub" "books" "bookssub";
        justify-items: start;
        row-gap: 0.35rem;
      }
      .hero-sub--doctrines { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
      .hero-doc-links { font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
      .hero-cta { max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.55rem 0.95rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
      .hero-cta-label { font-size: 0.9rem; }
      .hero-cta--ghost .hero-cta-label { font-size: 0.78rem; }

      .logo-panel {
        padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
        min-height: 130px;
      }

      .logo-panel-img {
        max-width: 220px;
      }

      .content-panel {
        padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
        gap: 0.75rem;
      }

      .hero-headline {
        font-size: 1.6rem;
      }

      /* Stack body + button vertically once the hero collapses to one column */
      .hero-body-row {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      .hero-body {
        max-width: 100%;
      }
    }
  </style>


  {picks.length > 0 && (
    <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="featured-picks">
      <div class="home-shell home-shell--wide">
        <h2 id="featured-picks" class="home-h2">Featured Picks</h2>
        <div class="home-picks">
          {picks.map((p) => (
            <SeriesCard
              skin={p.skin}
              href={p.href}
              title={p.title}
              description={p.deck}
              cta={p.cta}
              date={showDate(p.date)}
              location={p.location}
              symbol={p.symbol}
            />
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {recent.length > 0 && (
    <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="last-30-days">
      <div class="home-shell">
        <h2 id="last-30-days" class="home-h2">Last 30 Days</h2>
        <p class="home-sub">Added in the past month, filed by where each study lives. Open a section to see them.</p>
        <div class="home-recent">
          {recent.map((g) => (
            <details class="home-group" style={`--grp-accent: ${g.accent}`}>
              <summary>
                <span class="home-group-name">
                  <svg class="home-group-chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
                  <span class="home-group-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><Symbol name={g.symbol} size="1.05rem" /></span>{g.name} <span class="home-group-count">({g.items.length})</span>
                  <span class="home-group-cue"><span class="cue-closed">See list ▾</span><span class="cue-open">Hide list ▴</span></span>
                </span>
                <a class="home-group-all" href={g.href}>View all <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              </summary>
              <ul class="home-group-list">
                {g.items.map((it) => (
                  <li>
                    <a href={it.href}>
                      <span class="home-item-line">
                        <span class="home-item-title">{it.title}</span>
                        <span class="home-item-date">{showDate(it.date)}</span>
                      </span>
                      {it.deck && <span class="home-item-deck">{it.deck}</span>}
                    </a>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <!-- ============================================================
       THE WATCHMAN'S DESK — dispatch log (Homepage Desk + YouTube 1014).
       The last three letters/briefs as full-width rows: dateline + type
       tag | title + deck | call to action. Newest row leads.
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="wr-section" aria-label="The Watchman's Desk">
    <div class="wr-container">

      <div class="wr-header">
        <svg class="wr-tower" viewBox="0 0 120 160" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M60 4 L84 30 H36 Z" />
          <rect x="30" y="30" width="60" height="7" />
          <rect x="38" y="37" width="44" height="18" />
          <rect x="26" y="55" width="68" height="6" />
          <path d="M40 61 H80 L94 156 H26 Z M52 72 L45 146 H75 L68 72 Z" fill-rule="evenodd" />
          <path d="M46 84 L74 112 M74 84 L46 112 M44 118 L76 146 M76 118 L44 146" stroke-width="3" fill="none" />
        </svg>
        <p class="wr-eyebrow">★ Field Notes From the Wall ★</p>
        <h2 class="wr-title">The Watchman&rsquo;s Desk</h2>
        <a class="wr-archive-link" href="/watchmans-desk">Browse the archive &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <ol class="wr-log">
        {deskLog.map((e, i) => (
          <li>
            <a class:list={['wr-row', { 'wr-row--lead': i === 0 }]} href={e.href}>
              <span class="wr-stamp">
                <span class="wr-stamp-date">{e.dateline}</span>
                <span class="wr-stamp-kind">{e.kind}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="wr-row-body">
                <span class="wr-row-title">{e.title}</span>
                {e.deck && <span class="wr-row-deck">{e.deck}</span>}
                {i === 0 && e.tagline && <span class="wr-row-tagline">{e.tagline}</span>}
              </span>
              <span class="wr-row-cta">{e.cta} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       YOUTUBE — film strip. Channel on the left, the latest uploads on a
       sideways-scrolling strip. Every link leaves for YouTube in a new tab;
       nothing plays on the site.
       ============================================================ -->
  {videos.length > 0 && (
    <section class="yt-band" aria-label="Dutchman on YouTube">
      <div class="yt-inner">
        <div class="yt-channel">
          <a class="yt-avatar" href={CHANNEL_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Dutchman on YouTube">
            <img src="/images/nazar-144-avatar.jpg" alt="" width="120" height="120" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="yt-shimmer" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
          <p class="yt-name">Dutchman <span class="yt-dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span class="yt-handle">@Nazar-144</span></p>
          <a class="yt-subscribe" href={`${CHANNEL_URL}?sub_confirmation=1`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Subscribe <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>

        <div class="yt-strip" data-yt-strip>
          <button class="yt-arrow yt-arrow--prev" type="button" aria-label="Earlier videos" data-yt-prev hidden>&#8249;</button>
          <ul class="yt-reel" data-yt-reel>
            {videos.map((v) => (
              <li class="yt-frame">
                <a href={v.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                  <span class="yt-thumb">
                    <img src={v.thumb} alt="" width="480" height="270" loading="lazy" />
                    <svg class="yt-play" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="22" /><path d="M19 15 L35 24 L19 33 Z" /></svg>
                  </span>
                  <span class="yt-title">{v.title}</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <button class="yt-arrow yt-arrow--next" type="button" aria-label="More videos" data-yt-next hidden>&#8250;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <script>
    // Film-strip arrows: shown only when the reel overflows, scroll one frame.
    for (const strip of document.querySelectorAll('[data-yt-strip]')) {
      const reel = strip.querySelector('[data-yt-reel]');
      const prev = strip.querySelector('[data-yt-prev]');
      const next = strip.querySelector('[data-yt-next]');
      const step = () => (reel.querySelector('.yt-frame')?.getBoundingClientRect().width ?? 240) + 16;
      const sync = () => {
        const overflow = reel.scrollWidth > reel.clientWidth + 2;
        prev.hidden = next.hidden = !overflow;
        prev.disabled = reel.scrollLeft <= 2;
        next.disabled = reel.scrollLeft + reel.clientWidth >= reel.scrollWidth - 2;
      };
      prev.addEventListener('click', () => reel.scrollBy({ left: -step(), behavior: 'smooth' }));
      next.addEventListener('click', () => reel.scrollBy({ left: step(), behavior: 'smooth' }));
      reel.addEventListener('scroll', sync, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', sync);
      sync();
    }
  </script>


  <!-- ============================================================
       SCRIPTURE INSIGHT — one quiet strip: the latest posted insight,
       then a link into the full page. Renders NOTHING (no container, no
       placeholder) when there is no posted entry.
       ============================================================ -->
  {latestInsight && (
    <section class="si-strip" aria-label="Scripture Insight">
      <div class="si-strip-inner">
        <p class="si-strip-text">{latestInsight.text}</p>
        {latestInsight.blip && latestInsight.blip.trim() && (
          <p class="si-strip-blip">{latestInsight.blip}</p>
        )}
        {latestInsight.refs && latestInsight.refs.length > 0 && (
          <p class="si-strip-refs">{latestInsight.refs.join(' · ')}</p>
        )}
        <a class="si-strip-link" href="/close-to-the-hip">Close to the Hip <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <style>
    /* ── SCRIPTURE INSIGHT strip — quiet closer beneath the Desk. Same dark
       ground as the rail/desk sections; a single centered insight, not a hero. */
    .si-strip { background: #0a0a0a; border-top: 1px solid rgba(212,175,55,0.1); padding: 3rem 0 3.25rem; }
    .si-strip-inner { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2.5rem; text-align: center; }
    .si-strip-text { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #d8cdb4; margin: 0; }
    .si-strip-blip { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #8f8672; margin: 0.9rem 0 0; }
    .si-strip-refs { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #97854f; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; }
    .si-strip-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.4rem; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; color: #BA7517; text-decoration: none; transition: color .2s ease; }
    .si-strip-link:hover { color: #f0e0bf; }
    @media (max-width: 600px) { .si-strip-inner { padding: 0 1.25rem; } .si-strip { padding: 2.5rem 0 2.75rem; } }
  </style>

  <style>
    /* ============================================================
       FEATURED PICKS / LAST 30 DAYS — same dark ground the
       rail had. Card looks come from the skins; nothing here colors a card.
       ============================================================ */
    .home-band { background: #0a0a0a; padding: 2.75rem 0 0.5rem; }
    .home-shell { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2.5rem; }
    .home-h2 {
      font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.26em;
      text-transform: uppercase; font-variant: small-caps; color: #d4af37; text-align: center; margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    }
    .home-sub {
      font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: #a09078; text-align: center; margin: -0.9rem 0 1.4rem;
    }

    /* Featured Picks: up to ten compact cards, rows of five (1013 V20);
       rows of three on a tablet, one column on a phone. */
    .home-shell--wide { max-width: 80rem; }
    .home-picks { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.9rem; row-gap: 1.1rem; grid-auto-rows: 1fr; }

    /* Last 30 Days row symbol, in the section's own colour. */
    .home-group-symbol { display: inline-flex; vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-right: 0.45rem; color: var(--grp-accent); }

    /* Last 30 Days: closed dropdowns, a series-color bar on the left edge. */
    .home-recent { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; max-width: 52rem; margin: 0 auto; }
    .home-group {
      background: #141210; border: 1px solid rgba(201,169,97,0.14); border-left: 3px solid var(--grp-accent);
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .home-group summary {
      list-style: none; cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem; padding: 0.95rem 1.2rem;
    }
    .home-group summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .home-group summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--grp-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .home-group-name { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.12rem; color: #f5e6c8; }
    /* V4 (A6): the open cue — a gold chevron the size of the symbol (down when
       closed, up when open) and a small-caps SEE LIST / HIDE LIST after the count. */
    .home-group-chev { width: 1.15rem; height: 1.15rem; flex: none; color: #d4af37; margin-right: 0.45rem; vertical-align: -0.2em; transition: transform .2s ease; }
    .home-group[open] .home-group-chev { transform: rotate(180deg); }
    .home-group-cue {
      margin-left: 0.6rem; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.58rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      text-transform: uppercase; font-variant: small-caps; color: #a8925a; white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: 0.1em;
    }
    .home-group-cue .cue-open, .home-group[open] .home-group-cue .cue-closed { display: none; }
    .home-group[open] .home-group-cue .cue-open { display: inline; }
    .home-group summary { transition: background .15s ease; border-radius: 4px; }
    .home-group summary:hover { background: #1c1915; }
    .home-group-count { color: #a09078; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .home-group-all {
      flex: none; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 700; color: #c9a961; text-decoration: none;
    }
    .home-group-all:hover { color: #f5e6c8; }
    .home-group-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0 1.2rem 0.6rem; }
    .home-group-list li { border-top: 1px solid rgba(201,169,97,0.1); }
    .home-group-list a { display: block; padding: 0.7rem 0; text-decoration: none; }
    .home-item-line { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .home-item-title { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.3; color: #e8d9b8; }
    .home-group-list a:hover .home-item-title { color: #f0c450; }
    .home-item-date { flex: none; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.58rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8f8268; }
    .home-item-deck { display: block; margin-top: 0.2rem; font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.45; color: #a09078; }

    /* ============================================================
       THE WATCHMAN'S REPORT — field-notes band. Deliberately looks
       different from the muted-dark rail: red / cream / navy news look.
       ============================================================ */
    .wr-section {
      --wr-navy: #0a1d3a; --wr-navy-deep: #061230; --wr-red: #b8232a;
      --wr-red-deep: #8a1a20; --wr-cream: #f5f1e6; --wr-parchment: #ebe3cf;
      --wr-gold: #c9a961; --wr-ink-soft: #3a3a3a;
      background: #0a0a0a; padding: 3.25rem 0 4rem; border-top: 4px solid var(--wr-red);
    }
    .wr-container { max-width: 80rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2.5rem; }
    .wr-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .wr-eyebrow { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.3em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--wr-red); font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
    .wr-title { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem); color: var(--wr-cream); margin: 0; }
    /* Band-level archive link — section navigation, so it sits in the masthead
       under the title (not inside a card). Text link only: no fill, no border,
       no button padding. Tight to the title; the header's margin-bottom opens the
       larger break before the card row. House red on black, brightening to cream. */
    .wr-archive-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 0.55rem; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.28em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; color: var(--wr-red); text-decoration: none; transition: color .2s ease; }
    .wr-archive-link:hover { color: var(--wr-cream); }

    /* Faint watchtower behind the masthead — navy barely off the black. */
    .wr-header { position: relative; }
    .wr-header > :not(.wr-tower) { position: relative; }
    .wr-tower { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; width: 8rem; height: 11rem; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); fill: #0c1729; stroke: #0c1729; pointer-events: none; }

    /* Dispatch log — full width rows divided by thin red hairlines. */
    .wr-log { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(184,35,42,0.45); }
    .wr-log li { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(184,35,42,0.45); }
    .wr-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 1.75rem; align-items: center; padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 transparent; transition: box-shadow .2s ease, background-color .2s ease; }
    .wr-row:hover, .wr-row:focus-visible { box-shadow: inset 4px 0 0 var(--wr-red); background: rgba(10,29,58,0.28); outline: none; }
    .wr-stamp { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; align-self: start; padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem; background: var(--wr-navy); border-left: 2px solid var(--wr-red); }
    .wr-stamp-date { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: #ff6b6f; white-space: nowrap; }
    .wr-stamp-kind { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.56rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: #f08a8d; white-space: nowrap; }
    .wr-row-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; min-width: 0; }
    .wr-row-title { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--wr-parchment); }
    .wr-row:hover .wr-row-title { color: #fff; }
    .wr-row-deck { font-family: 'Crimson Text', Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.45; color: #b5aa92; }
    .wr-row-tagline { font-family: 'Crimson Text', Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.4; color: #e2555b; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
    .wr-row-cta { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.64rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e2555b; white-space: nowrap; }
    .wr-row:hover .wr-row-cta { color: var(--wr-cream); }
    .wr-row--lead { padding-top: 1.75rem; padding-bottom: 1.75rem; }
    .wr-row--lead .wr-row-title { font-size: 1.7rem; }

    /* ============================================================
       YOUTUBE — film strip band
       ============================================================ */
    .yt-band { background: #050505; border-top: 1px solid rgba(212,175,55,0.12); padding: 3rem 0 3.25rem; }
    .yt-inner { max-width: 80rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2.5rem; align-items: center; }
    .yt-channel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
    .yt-avatar { position: relative; display: block; width: 120px; height: 120px; border-radius: 50%; overflow: hidden; border: 2px solid #c9a961; box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(0,0,0,0.6); }
    .yt-avatar img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
    /* The moon's path on the water: a soft band of light lines over the
       reflection column, drifting slowly so the water seems to move. */
    .yt-shimmer {
      position: absolute; left: 34%; right: 34%; top: 44%; bottom: 0;
      background: repeating-linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,250,235,0) 0 3px, rgba(255,250,235,0.45) 3px 4px, rgba(255,250,235,0) 4px 7px);
      background-size: 100% 14px;
      mix-blend-mode: screen;
      -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 70% at 50% 40%, #000 30%, transparent 75%);
              mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 70% at 50% 40%, #000 30%, transparent 75%);
      animation: yt-shimmer 4.5s ease-in-out infinite;
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    @keyframes yt-shimmer {
      0%   { background-position: 0 0;    opacity: 0.35; transform: scaleX(1); }
      50%  { background-position: 0 7px;  opacity: 0.75; transform: scaleX(1.12); }
      100% { background-position: 0 14px; opacity: 0.35; transform: scaleX(1); }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .yt-shimmer { animation: none; opacity: 0.35; } }
    .yt-name { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.74rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #ebe3cf; }
    .yt-dot { color: #b8232a; }
    .yt-handle { color: #a09078; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: none; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .yt-subscribe { display: inline-block; margin-top: 0.25rem; padding: 0.6rem 1.3rem; border-radius: 3px; background: #b8232a; color: #fff; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 0.66rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none; transition: background-color .2s ease; }
    .yt-subscribe:hover, .yt-subscribe:focus-visible { background: #d02e36; }

    /* The strip: dark film with sprocket holes along the top and bottom edge. */
    .yt-strip { position: relative; min-width: 0; padding: 22px 0; background: #121110; border-radius: 4px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(212,175,55,0.08); }
    .yt-strip::before, .yt-strip::after {
      content: ''; position: absolute; left: 10px; right: 10px; height: 8px;
      background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(235,227,207,0.82) 0 11px, transparent 11px 24px);
      -webkit-mask-image: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #000 0 11px, transparent 11px 24px);
      border-radius: 2px; pointer-events: none;
    }
    .yt-strip::before { top: 7px; }
    .yt-strip::after { bottom: 7px; }
    .yt-reel { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; display: flex; gap: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; scroll-snap-type: x mandatory; scrollbar-width: none; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }
    .yt-reel::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
    .yt-frame { flex: 0 0 15rem; scroll-snap-align: start; }
    .yt-frame a { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; text-decoration: none; }
    .yt-thumb { position: relative; display: block; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 2px; background: #000; transition: transform .25s ease, box-shadow .25s ease; }
    .yt-thumb img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
    .yt-play { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; width: 2.6rem; height: 2.6rem; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0.85); opacity: 0; transition: opacity .25s ease, transform .25s ease; }
    .yt-play circle { fill: rgba(0,0,0,0.55); stroke: #d4af37; stroke-width: 2; }
    .yt-play path { fill: #f5e6c8; }
    .yt-frame a:hover .yt-thumb, .yt-frame a:focus-visible .yt-thumb { transform: translateY(-4px); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(212,175,55,0.7), 0 10px 26px rgba(212,175,55,0.28); }
    .yt-frame a:hover .yt-play, .yt-frame a:focus-visible .yt-play { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1); }
    .yt-frame a:focus-visible { outline: none; }
    .yt-title { font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.3; color: #ebe3cf; display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 2; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; overflow: hidden; }
    .yt-frame a:hover .yt-title { color: #f0c450; }
    .yt-arrow { position: absolute; top: 50%; z-index: 2; width: 2.2rem; height: 2.2rem; margin-top: -1.6rem; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid rgba(212,175,55,0.5); background: rgba(5,5,5,0.88); color: #d4af37; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1; cursor: pointer; }
    .yt-arrow--prev { left: -1.1rem; }
    .yt-arrow--next { right: -1.1rem; }
    .yt-arrow:disabled { opacity: 0.3; cursor: default; }
    .yt-arrow:not(:disabled):hover { background: #d4af37; color: #050505; }

    /* ============================================================
       RESPONSIVE
       ============================================================ */
    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .yt-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.75rem; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 768px), (pointer: coarse) {
      .yt-arrow { display: none; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 680px) {
      /* Phone: the dateline sits above the title. */
      .wr-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.6rem; padding: 1.1rem 0.75rem; }
      .wr-stamp { flex-direction: row; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.75rem; align-self: start; }
      .wr-row--lead .wr-row-title { font-size: 1.45rem; }
      .wr-row-title { font-size: 1.15rem; }
      .yt-frame { flex-basis: 72%; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 1100px) { .home-picks { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
    @media (max-width: 640px) { .home-picks { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .home-shell, .wr-container, .yt-inner { padding: 0 1rem; }
      .wr-section { padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem; }
      .home-group summary { padding: 0.9rem 1rem; }
      .home-group-list { padding: 0 1rem 0.5rem; }
    }
  </style>



</BaseLayout>
